#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050677 :topic/id #uuid "5e132315-9606-5b30-bee3-61f0209d40c4" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152273 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151961 :question/id #uuid "45688683-2788-58bd-8cf5-80feab863551" :question/math-academy-id "e-6566" :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n- $y'' + (y-1)y'+x = 2$\n\n- $y''+y'=x \\cos x$\n\n- $yy'' - y'+ 9 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "A second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x)y'' + b(x)y' + c(x) y = f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\ny'' + (y-1)y'+x = 2\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $(y-1)y'.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\ny''+y'=x \\cos x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x) = 1, b(x) = 1, c(x) = 0,$ and $f(x) = x\\cos{x}.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\nyy'' - y'+ 9 = 0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $yy''.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a926134-0870-5528-985d-2c92e71158f4" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152627 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a90d15b6-e285-5a3a-aad1-d8cdfca3e7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150270} {:answer/id #uuid "b8547879-45cf-5ca3-9142-0eb0e137b41a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150271} {:answer/id #uuid "360ccc44-5d9a-585b-b2f0-abdf941c39e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150272} {:answer/id #uuid "50ed892d-f16c-5db0-877a-802c142b6955" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150273} {:answer/id #uuid "632744cb-8b77-529e-92cc-aafa46802692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "360ccc44-5d9a-585b-b2f0-abdf941c39e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150272} :answer-field/id #uuid "5df027ae-08a8-5287-a5b5-c3436f8c0d69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150269}] :question/id #uuid "f1ebf17d-0b25-58c1-9a31-4457dac88f37" :question/math-academy-id "q-64961" :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n1. $y^{″} + 2y^{′} + 5y = 0$\n2. $3y^{″} + y^{2}y^{′} + 4 = 0$\n3. $y^{″} - xy = x$" :question/worked-solution "A second-order ODE is linear when the coefficients of $y'',$ $y',$ and $y$ depend only on $x,$ and $y$ and its derivatives occur to the first power.\n\n- Equation I, $y''+2y'+5y=0,$ is linear, with constant coefficients.\n- Equation II, $3y''+y^2y'+4=0,$ is nonlinear because the coefficient $y^2$ of $y'$ depends on $y.$\n- Equation III, $y''-xy=x,$ is linear: its coefficients $1,$ $0,$ and $-x$ depend only on $x.$\n\nTherefore the correct answer is **I and III only**."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152631 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86fd8b29-1a8e-50e5-847b-7bd9b8eeb478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150294} {:answer/id #uuid "c1dcc3e8-2a21-5da1-868c-d504a80dcc93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150295} {:answer/id #uuid "071967a7-a546-5a79-9fd3-bcbc4a208135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150296} {:answer/id #uuid "38282a72-d2ca-5f1c-912a-336c427ae641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150297} {:answer/id #uuid "5af276a2-71b7-51fb-b330-ff62cce1cca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38282a72-d2ca-5f1c-912a-336c427ae641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150297} :answer-field/id #uuid "c017f9a9-e0fa-57e9-83d1-ec9c008a3ae8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150293}] :question/id #uuid "e59648fc-66f7-5081-a7c6-b8e94dcbd9e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-65008" :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\n1. $xy^{″} + 2y^{′} + (\\cos x)y = 0$\n2. $3y^{″} + x^{2}y^{′} + xy = 4$\n3. $y^{″} - yy^{′} = x$" :question/worked-solution "A second-order ODE is linear when it has the form $a(x)y''+b(x)y'+c(x)y=f(x),$ with coefficients depending only on $x$ and with $a(x)\\ne0$ on the interval considered.\n\n- Equation I, $xy''+2y'+(\\cos x)y=0,$ is linear on any interval avoiding $x=0.$\n- Equation II, $3y''+x^2y'+xy=4,$ is linear, since all its coefficients depend only on $x.$\n- Equation III, $y''-yy'=x,$ is nonlinear because the coefficient $-y$ of $y'$ depends on $y.$\n\nTherefore the correct answer is **I and II only**."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265953 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86d0fa0c-d83e-5302-8b19-931a556d2598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463874} {:answer/id #uuid "5f240d2f-1e1c-5d49-baec-e89948422632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f240d2f-1e1c-5d49-baec-e89948422632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463875} :answer-field/id #uuid "79ca8d72-13b8-5039-a525-2d310ad8c033" :answer-field/key "$2{y}^{″}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}-y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464871} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f52e27e-69b6-5665-a21e-03f68b051fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463876} {:answer/id #uuid "a89b723d-942b-536a-99f1-180995a49f0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f52e27e-69b6-5665-a21e-03f68b051fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463876} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c322dd1-207e-5f01-a185-f2cc43f25df4" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+y{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464872} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3971c54-39c4-5514-becd-d741348b687e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463878} {:answer/id #uuid "2f404fad-6d9a-5bce-9290-c3cc1f239e76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f404fad-6d9a-5bce-9290-c3cc1f239e76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463879} :answer-field/id #uuid "f01fab60-26ab-58e5-a863-3b739a2c5149" :answer-field/key "$x{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "114cf182-dccf-5764-a411-6c6c3328247d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130670" :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}-y=1\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=2,b(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,c(x)=-1,$ and $f(x)=1.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{′}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\nx{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=x,b(x)=0,c(x)={x}^{2},$ and $f(x)={e}^{x}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $2{y}^{″}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}-y=1$; $x{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265954 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "579c4389-1f02-5274-8ef3-8ddb9e4c467e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463880} {:answer/id #uuid "e663fafa-9f14-55d5-96ad-2c10d31e9978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e663fafa-9f14-55d5-96ad-2c10d31e9978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463881} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebbcca07-c4cf-5d12-95bd-1a28dfe3407d" :answer-field/key "$(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464874} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de69a75-9c0f-52d9-9354-fc0f795fdd9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463882} {:answer/id #uuid "fa25ee79-e03c-544e-a40d-6452f7a7cd34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4de69a75-9c0f-52d9-9354-fc0f795fdd9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463882} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ee4df8d-ba88-55d3-b4f4-b9365c7e3811" :answer-field/key "${y}^{3}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}-xy=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464875} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aef3aa88-07ae-5c22-b0e4-3dcd060e653f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463884} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b6dc71-fa1f-5546-a7a1-52cd8f76be5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aef3aa88-07ae-5c22-b0e4-3dcd060e653f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463884} :answer-field/id #uuid "920346ba-105f-56c1-baa3-ede3853ae5b9" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+xy{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d7e46e30-10b0-546e-b7af-e3d72616cbd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-130671" :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=2\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,b(x)=-x,c(x)=1,$ and $f(x)=2.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}-xy=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term ${y}^{3}{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+xy{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $xy{y}^{′}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=2$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265955 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d90b07b-3b2f-5dd7-ae06-6bd4d25eaaaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463886} {:answer/id #uuid "41052ad9-08e4-5109-873f-da03122a643d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d90b07b-3b2f-5dd7-ae06-6bd4d25eaaaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463886} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0b765e3-1d1e-5789-ba6d-dddb94ca8a11" :answer-field/key "${e}^{2y}{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+3=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464877} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0be1a6c-64d1-5b97-a693-794b4829a6c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463888} {:answer/id #uuid "40011b59-21dd-5ba2-87ee-913716a1d1ca" :answer/type {: