x)=-x,c(x)=1,$ and $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y{y}^{′}=0\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{′}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{y}{y}^{″}+y=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $\\frac{1}{y}{y}^{″}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357562 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09a469b2-5896-588d-9b5f-f86452b44eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469632} {:answer/id #uuid "aca4c5d2-3985-5df0-8512-b4a193218a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09a469b2-5896-588d-9b5f-f86452b44eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469632} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2f92d40-06fd-5963-9b61-c9a8f2d37df8" :answer-field/key "$2{y}^{2}{y}^{″}-{e}^{x}{y}^{′}=x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470428} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7732c50a-196e-5bd4-ae46-9604b54c4cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469634} {:answer/id #uuid "4c2401c4-e763-54a9-90ce-bd5138b0907a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c2401c4-e763-54a9-90ce-bd5138b0907a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469635} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c4a0149-404f-5dda-a8e0-57d0e7983147" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470429} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c20331be-786e-5ec8-92b5-cf500b578551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469636} {:answer/id #uuid "c09b531f-230e-59c8-a5d3-13154d41383b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c09b531f-230e-59c8-a5d3-13154d41383b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469637} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e6c792f-fb4d-56c6-a87c-d0da2370a750" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+17y=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470430}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d6e8b60c-c6c9-5753-b254-94e3e9635292" :question/math-academy-id "q-93721" :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n2{y}^{2}{y}^{″}-{e}^{x}{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $2{y}^{2}{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=\\frac{1}{x},b(x)=1,c(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ and $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+17y=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=1,b(x)=0,c(x)=17,$ and $f(x)=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x;\n$$ ${y}^{″}+17y=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ only."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Linear ODEs"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152274 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151960 :question/id #uuid "f0520e86-8df9-5090-8d5c-761a4ba20583" :question/math-academy-id "e-6565" :question/problem "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.\n\n- $\\, (2-\\sin(x)) y'' + x y' + y = 0$\n\n- $\\,y'' + 6y' + 9y = 3e^x$\n\n- $\\,y'' + x^3 y - 8 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x)y'' + b(x)y' + c(x) y = f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x) = 0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n(2-\\sin(x)) y'' + x y' + y = 0\n$$\n\nis homogeneous since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x) = 0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\ny'' + 6y' + 9y = 3e^x\n$$\n\nis inhomogeneous since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x) = 3e^x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\ny'' + x^3 y - 8 = 0\n$$\n\nin the form $ay'' + by' + cy = f,$ we have\n\n$$\ny'' + x^3 y = 8.\n$$\n\nThis equation is inhomogeneous since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x) = 8,$ which is different from zero."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90930e15-0827-5e0b-82cf-98263fc756d6" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152571 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a68fe6b-8f74-5590-aaa7-71b814ce5ca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755740} {:answer/id #uuid "19e20688-36bb-54e2-b5b8-e95a822affc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19e20688-36bb-54e2-b5b8-e95a822affc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755741} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd09c577-a9ca-5574-8285-ee6573981581" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755739} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b08593cd-ad99-5e19-9bd4-3ad4d6915c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755743} {:answer/id #uuid "ea30811a-0c03-5682-b3f9-3324c9d2b467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b08593cd-ad99-5e19-9bd4-3ad4d6915c79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755743} :answer-field/id #uuid "45c63372-991c-5aed-a75c-3be1e0befb37" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755742} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fe9cad6-e923-580c-8231-305568e095e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755746} {:answer/id #uuid "079218f5-e963-5141-9196-aefababe086a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fe9cad6-e923-580c-8231-305568e095e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755746} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b502565-9479-5327-98c5-d51943c30c22" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+xy-2x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755745}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e7830240-8585-5e21-ba7a-c44cace370a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-337919" :question/problem "Select all homogeneous second-order linear differential equations.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){y}^{″}-x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=2\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=2,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy-2x=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy=2x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=2x,$ which is different from zero."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152572 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38c119f8-87a8-5e89-883c-2e545edee1a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755749} {:answer/id #uuid "43fe3b14-c65d-5964-aab8-9b342ccfcf4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43fe3b14-c65d-5964-aab8-9b342ccfcf4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755750} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3472571-49c5-53bf-8140-7f8e6ac3e9d8" :answer-field/key "${x}^{2}{y}^{″}+3x{y}^{′}-y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755748} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e85ac65-0f39-509b-a3cc-a3b56168ff10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755752} {:answer/id #uuid "4d9b1025-387b-5897-acc6-a136d8432ba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e85ac65-0f39-509b-a3cc-a3b56168ff10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755752} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e25eeca-5c2d-52ee-9ddc-cdbc305e2c66" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+y={e}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "608d3316-2cf3-5c08-9485-171725600c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755755} {:answer/id #uuid "de0b6529-d2bd-505e-8c9b-451b89e2d8d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "608d3316-2cf3-5c08-9485-171725600c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755755} :answer-field/id #uuid "d55bb1b8-4c53-5802-b84b-7bc89bb4c704" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y+x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4e93ecbe-42b9-5aed-a2ce-1b2b418237f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-337990" :question/problem "Select all homogeneous second-order linear differential equations.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+3x{y}^{′}-y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+y={e}^{x}\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)={e}^{x},$ which is different from zero.\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y+x=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y=-x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-x,$ which is different from zero."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311903 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8acbb98-2a4d-5203-99d2-be4abc6a7848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755758} {:answer/id #uuid "ec33ec02-afae-5b20-8d84-fcbb3427c98e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8acbb98-2a4d-5203-99d2-be4abc6a7848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755758} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd1fc782-b07e-5932-99e9-05a2c3204147" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+6y=7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffae9ce5-8cc3-566d-b1af-7d7546f31911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755761} {:answer/id #uuid "8d108623-7585-5ac4-ae68-6c29a4bdd931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d108623-7585-5ac4-ae68-6c29a4bdd931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755762} :answer-field/id #uuid "7135fed3-ee7a-56f5-86d0-5f188c9b587d" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x){y}^{″}+(1-x){y}^{′}-4y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8be7acb1-ac2f-5e66-a056-bb6e493ade6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755764} {:answer/id #uuid "aec0fa71-df2e-5d77-a08d-7782e071e911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8be7acb1-ac2f-5e66-a056-bb6e493ade6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755764} :answer-field/id #uuid "b45d5c50-4b5d-5240-9710-41b2b9db9bf1" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+xy+{x}^{3}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755763}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6d738a1f-befb-5d33-811f-bc5d7b9e6626" :question/math-academy-id "q-337996" :question/problem "Select all homogeneous second-order linear differential equations.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+6y=7\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=7,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x){y}^{″}+(1-x){y}^{′}-4y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy+{x}^{3}=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy=-{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-{x}^{3},$ which is different from zero."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30dc4c1c-53ea-5e83-ade5-bdb23b31c573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755776} {:answer/id #uuid "f7fdc313-69b7-5a8e-a9df-e67dbc66fbef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7fdc313-69b7-5a8e-a9df-e67dbc66fbef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755777} :answer-field/id #uuid "0037f8ee-88e5-5d1d-a24b-4317e71683d5" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+xy=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755775} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edd8f22d-798b-54b0-9fba-963dbc5dee3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755779} {:answer/id #uuid "0e461b01-8c9b-5008-87fc-90ada1efeb56" :answer/type {:db/id 