me{cos}⁡(x){y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+xy=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-2y=4x\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=4x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9119a1e-cd12-515d-b0cd-05956c355688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755785} {:answer/id #uuid "8e1594d2-0413-504b-8ff5-be5e487d2c24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9119a1e-cd12-515d-b0cd-05956c355688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755785} :answer-field/id #uuid "3942431c-e386-552c-9da2-9600116cfc8d" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15466616-c2da-5495-b6f6-1dc5356412d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755788} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4dcb5d-ab00-598c-b3ed-296e1e17f068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f4dcb5d-ab00-598c-b3ed-296e1e17f068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755789} :answer-field/id #uuid "056ff69c-7495-5e6a-8bca-2b9c9c21ad74" :answer-field/key "$(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "377c04e2-2f80-51da-9b31-a7dcf84b120c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755791} {:answer/id #uuid "d98bafcb-d884-5ded-8142-f4cc9f7b1a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "377c04e2-2f80-51da-9b31-a7dcf84b120c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755791} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1ae30e0-a3a9-52ef-a3d8-cb50770ad534" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+xy-{e}^{x}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "71bb7beb-a9ec-524e-b310-db15c4e11f3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-338023" :question/problem "Select all homogeneous second-order linear differential equations.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ which is different from zero.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy-{e}^{x}=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)={e}^{x},$ which is different from zero."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2552a4d9-f78f-5d7c-ba54-94ce2e3d49c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755803} {:answer/id #uuid "938ee41a-af05-5b09-873f-ba86a46017f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "938ee41a-af05-5b09-873f-ba86a46017f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755804} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9251bf7-8183-5579-89dd-1bad45029dc2" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+(x-2){y}^{′}+y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755802} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf5c5d6f-5ccb-5d4f-bc88-5ab55e86ea42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755806} {:answer/id #uuid "a15763ad-367c-54f7-b3f3-1fbdbb663026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a15763ad-367c-54f7-b3f3-1fbdbb663026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755807} :answer-field/id #uuid "076df855-d1d0-58a5-bdca-0e10426c7bcc" :answer-field/key "$({x}^{2}+1){y}^{″}-4x{y}^{′}+3y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186755805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uui