alue "{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{x-1}y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440918} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6650bd-3f73-576d-b334-45546a281ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+xy={x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ec291cf-419e-545a-91fe-9ee555957888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+xy=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440911} :answer-field/id #uuid "b50eac1f-2fd4-5e79-99ef-7e7a92a52cdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4ce39611-61f7-5873-a772-9d52755c9e24" :question/math-academy-id "q-130992" :question/problem "For the differential equation $2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+xy={x}^{2}-x,$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+xy=0.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Associated Homogeneous Equation of a Second-Order Inhomogeneous ODE"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152276 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151962 :question/id #uuid "1826d315-cef0-5b5f-b654-61733a63bf2f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6567" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\n- $x^2y'' + xy' = x+2$\n\n- $9y'' + 4y = e^x, \\quad y(0) = 1,  \\quad  y'(4)= 1$\n\n- $y''+xy'+x^2y= \\sin x, \\quad y(1) = 0,  \\quad  y'(1)= 5$" :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem.**\n\nWith this in mind, let's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- System I is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- System II is not an initial value problem because it consists of a differential equation together with two conditions in *different* locations, $x=0$ and $x=4.$ So this is a **boundary value problem**, not an initial value problem.\n\n- System III is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d0a7ede-b896-56c6-9b60-a6aec8eff9e8" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152632 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e77d06e-75de-5efc-a31a-08ab5cd28827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460125} {:answer/id #uuid "d7273db4-f030-554b-9eb4-1f8ad7088e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7273db4-f030-554b-9eb4-1f8ad7088e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460126} :answer-field/id #uuid "7255451a-6f73-5904-b058-7ec744515ab6" :answer-field/key "$x{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y$ $={x}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ $\\,y(1)$ $=0,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(1)$ $=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460929} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1476747-7cd7-5321-b84b-6e1235b6e7e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218646012