ial equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$).\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=1$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The third system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b12ca010-23c7-5c1b-8b4c-56840bb07736" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473070} {:answer/id #uuid "6b05e278-5bae-5e61-b32f-14598a9387a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b05e278-5bae-5e61-b32f-14598a9387a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473071} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed18b99e-c355-5c3f-b3e5-3b1f0558a889" :answer-field/key "${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y$ $=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ $\\,y(4)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(4)$ $=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473930} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb1b2585-68f4-53b5-9ec6-8bc4769a9d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473072} {:answer/id #uuid "733c8d21-4cf3-55af-8e1b-fa9735e99d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb1b2585-68f4-53b5-9ec6-8bc4769a9d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :ans